# occurred_at is a time.Time, which reads itself and reports a plain error with
# no field on it. Walked as an ordinary struct, "tuesday" is answered with the
# word object, and the rule an RFC 3339 timestamp is held to is never said.

title: a type that reads itself is walked as though it did not
file: internal/ledgerhttp/decode.go
run: go test -count=1 -run TestABadTimestampNamesTheFieldAndTheShapeATimestampTakes -v ./internal/ledgerhttp/
--- before
	case reflect.PointerTo(t).Implements(jsonUnmarshaler):
	case t.Kind() == reflect.Struct:
--- after
	// negative control: a type that reads itself is walked field by field
	case t.Kind() == reflect.Struct:
